class:: BoundedWalk
summary:: Triggered random walk with explicit boundary and increment rules
categories:: UGens>Generators>Stochastic>Processes
related:: Guides/Stochastica, Classes/OUProcess, Classes/TBrownRand

description::

A Bounded Walk is a discrete-time random walk where the accumulating state is strictly confined between minimum and maximum limits, typically bouncing (folding) or wrapping upon collision. Mathematically, it prevents the variance of the random walk from growing to infinity. Conceptually, it is highly useful for generative sequencing, allowing a melody or parameter to wander endlessly, taking relative steps up or down, while guaranteeing it will never exceed the designated musical register or parameter range.

Adds a uniform, normal, or Cauchy increment on each rising trigger and applies an explicit reflect, wrap, clip, resample, or absorb boundary rule. Resampling stops after 64 attempts and then clips.

Unlike link::Classes/TBrownRand::, BoundedWalk has deterministic local seeding, rising-edge reset, several increment distributions, and named boundary semantics.

subsection:: Boundary comparison

image::bounded-walk-boundaries.png#The same seeded uniform increments under three rules: reflect at left, wrap at center, and absorb at right. Reflection reverses overshoot, wrapping jumps to the opposite edge, and absorption remains at the first boundary reached.::

classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: trig
Take one random-walk step on a rising edge.
argument:: step
Absolute uniform half-width, normal deviation, or Cauchy scale.
argument:: lo
Lower boundary.
argument:: hi
Upper boundary. When not above code::lo::, output holds at code::lo::.
argument:: boundary
0 reflect, 1 wrap, 2 clip, 3 bounded resample, 4 absorb.
argument:: distribution
0 uniform, 1 normal, 2 Cauchy.
argument:: initial
Initial value processed by the selected boundary rule.
argument:: seed
Init-rate local seed.
argument:: reset
Restore initial state, absorption status, and seed on a rising edge.
returns:: One audio-rate bounded state.

method:: kr
Control-rate version with the same arguments.

instancemethods::

examples::

code::
(
{ BoundedWalk.kr(Impulse.kr(12)).poll }.play
)
::

code::
(
{ SinOsc.ar(BoundedWalk.kr(Impulse.kr(20), 0.08, 0, 1).linexp(0, 1, 100, 3000), 0, 0.08) }.play
)
::

code::
(
{ Pan2.ar(Decay2.ar(Impulse.ar(8), 0.001, 0.1), BoundedWalk.kr(Impulse.kr(8), 0.3)) * 0.1 }.play
)
::

code::
// Wandering Pentatonic Melodies
(
{
    var trig, walk, scale, degree, freq, sig;
    trig = Impulse.kr([6,12]);
    // A random walk that safely bounces off its register boundaries
    walk = BoundedWalk.kr(trig, 1.0, lo: 0, hi: 14);
    scale = [0, 2, 4, 7, 9];
    degree = walk.round(1);
    freq = (DegreeToKey.kr(LocalBuf.newFrom(scale), degree, 12) + 60).midicps;
    sig = SinOsc.ar(freq) * EnvGen.kr(Env.perc(0.01, 0.2), trig);
    Pan2.ar(sig * 0.2)
}.play;
)
::
